BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Meet Nina LaCour\, Author of Meet Me in the Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T170000
DTSTAMP:20261122T201115Z
UID:smcl-6aea2102de685359098d9fdf@local-events
DESCRIPTION:New Orleans\, 1944. Odette has always been one of the Honore s
 isters\, glamorous and admired in their Creole community. But while Odette
 ’s older sisters are content to be wives and mothers\, Odette has always
  wanted something else. It is only with her beloved cousin\, Delphine\, th
 at Odette can tell her secret: she is in love with a woman\, and she longs
  to be an artist. Delphine has a secret lover\, too\, a white man. In the 
 hidden garden they’ve discovered\, Odette and Delphine can dream of futu
 res full of passion and freedom.  \n\nBut five years later\, Odette's 
 life is nothing like what she'd planned. She's a widowed mother\, living i
 n Los Angeles\, and she and Delphine\, who is passing as white\, have spir
 aled away from each other. When Delphine reaches a breaking point\, Odette
  must make a shattering choice to try to hold her family together.\n\nProf
 ound and expansive\, a story of love and longing\, art and motherhood\, fr
 iendship and desire\, Meet Me in the Garden  is a decades-spanning tour 
 de force\, inspired by the author’s family and tracing the history of th
 e Great Migration.\n\nGiveaway copies of Meet Me in the Garden will be av
 ailable on a first-come first-serve basis at the event while supplies last
 .\n\nNina LaCour is the bestselling\, Michael L. Printz Award and Lambda L
 iterary Award-winning author of picture books\, a chapter book series\, yo
 ung adult novels\, and adult literary fiction. Her novel We Are Okay was n
 amed one of TIME Magazine’s Top 100 YA Novels of All Time. Her two adult
  literary novels\, Yerba Buena and Meet Me in the Garden were Book of the 
 Month Club selections chosen as Indie Next Picks by independent bookseller
 s around the country. Garnering starred reviews from Kirkus\, Publishers W
 eekly\, BookPage\, Booklist\, and others\, Nina’s books have been transl
 ated into over a dozen languages. She lives in San Francisco with her fami
 ly.\n\nRegistration is encouraged\, but not required.\n\nAges: 12-18\nRegi
 stration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aea2102
 de685359098d9fdf\nLast synced: 2026-11-22 12:11 PST
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aea2102de685359098d9fdf
END:VEVENT
